      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks like a possible error, so I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times a day is **6400 mg/day**. That's twice the labeled maximum of 3200 mg/day, which is already the upper limit for prescription use.\n\nAt this dose there's a much higher risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, especially in a 70-year-old patient. It also matches a common mistake: writing the daily total as the per-dose amount.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **400 mg four times daily** (1600 mg/day total)\n2. **800 mg four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n3. **Another dose**\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, confirm that and give a short reason. I'll then enter it with a note recording your confirmation, though it would also be wise to involve pharmacy."
      }
