       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as you confirmed it: **ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth, four times daily** (Order ID: ORD-0001).\n\nThe order includes a note for pharmacy. It says the dose is twice the labeled maximum, both per dose and per day, that you confirmed it after a warning, and that no reason was given. It also asks a pharmacist to check the order before it's dispensed. Pharmacy may contact you, and you can speed that up by giving them the reason.\n\nIf you continue at this dose, it would be worth considering:\n- **Stomach protection:** a PPI to protect against GI bleeding\n- **Monitoring:** checking kidney function (BMP), CBC, and blood pressure\n- **Other drugs:** avoiding anticoagulants, steroids, and other NSAIDs at the same time\n\nIf you meant 400 mg or 800 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order. I can't cancel orders myself, so you'd need to discontinue ORD-0001."
